{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardTableauAxialDistance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardTableauAxialDistance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardTableauSpectral"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.cellContent_diag_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.cellContent_diag_step","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauAxialDistance.lean#L104-L108","doc":"The two cells of a diagonal step have **equal content** — so `diag_gap` is exactly the statement\nthat a zero axial distance cannot occur between consecutive entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.not_consecutive_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.not_consecutive_diag","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauAxialDistance.lean#L96-L102","doc":"**Consecutive entries are never on a diagonal step.**  The `d = 1` case of \"consecutive entries\nnever share a content\", and the one the seminormal denominators hit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.diag_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.diag_gap","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauAxialDistance.lean#L67-L94","doc":"**A diagonal step gains at least two.**\n\nIf `(r,c)` and `(r+1,c+1)` are both cells then the intermediate cell `(r,c+1)` exists — row `r` is\nat least as long as row `r+1` — and its entry is strictly between the other two, by `row_incr` then\n`col_incr`.  Hence the outer entries differ by `≥ 2`.\n\nThe strength of \"two\" rather than \"one\" is what makes this usable: it is exactly what forbids\nconsecutive entries on a diagonal, and hence what makes the seminormal denominators nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.toEquiv_entryAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.toEquiv_entryAt","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauAxialDistance.lean#L63-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.entryAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StandardTableau.entryAt","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauAxialDistance.lean#L59-L61","doc":"The entry occupying a given cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.mem_cells_of_le_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.mem_cells_of_le_col","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StandardTableauAxialDistance.lean#L46-L53","doc":"**A Young diagram is closed leftward within a row.** ","signatureChunk":0}]}